Now I have a comprehensive understanding of Better Auth's account management capabilities. Let me compile a complete report of my findings.

---

## Better Auth Account Management Capabilities Report

Based on my exploration of the Better Auth documentation repository at `/Users/orksys/Projects/docs-worktrees/better-auth/`, here is a comprehensive overview of all available account management features and their API methods:

---

### 1. Profile Updates (Name, Image)

**Client-side method:**
```typescript
// Update user information (name and image)
await authClient.updateUser({
    image: "https://example.com/image.jpg", // URL or base64
    name: "John Doe",
})
```

**Server-side API:**
```typescript
await auth.api.updateUser({
    body: {
        name: "New Name",
        image: "https://..."
    },
    headers: await headers()
})
```

---

### 2. Password Management

#### Change Password (requires current session)
```typescript
await authClient.changePassword({
    newPassword: "newpassword1234",
    currentPassword: "oldpassword1234",
    revokeOtherSessions: true // optional - invalidates other sessions
})
```

#### Set Password (server-side only, for OAuth users without passwords)
```typescript
await auth.api.setPassword({
    body: {
        newPassword: "new-password",
    },
    headers: await headers()
})
```

#### Verify Password (server-side only)
```typescript
await auth.api.verifyPassword({
    body: {
        password: "user-password"
    },
    headers: await headers()
})
```

#### Reset Password (forgot password flow)
```typescript
// Request password reset
await authClient.requestPasswordReset({
    email: "john.doe@example.com",
    redirectTo: "https://example.com/reset-password"
})

// Reset with token
await authClient.resetPassword({
    newPassword: "password1234",
    token: "verification-token"
})
```

**Server configuration:**
```typescript
export const auth = betterAuth({
    emailAndPassword: {
        enabled: true,
        sendResetPassword: async ({ user, url, token }, request) => {
            // Send reset email
        },
        onPasswordReset: async ({ user }, request) => {
            // Callback after successful reset
        },
        resetPasswordTokenExpiresIn: 3600 // seconds (default: 1 hour)
    }
})
```

---

### 3. Email Changes & Verification

#### Change Email
```typescript
await authClient.changeEmail({
    newEmail: "new-email@email.com",
    callbackURL: "/dashboard"
})
```

**Server configuration:**
```typescript
export const auth = betterAuth({
    user: {
        changeEmail: {
            enabled: true,
            // Optional: require confirmation from current email
            sendChangeEmailConfirmation: async ({ user, newEmail, url, token }, request) => {
                // Send confirmation to CURRENT email
            },
            // Optional: skip verification if current email is unverified
            updateEmailWithoutVerification: true
        }
    },
    emailVerification: {
        sendVerificationEmail: async ({ user, url, token }) => {
            // Send verification email
        }
    }
})
```

#### Email Verification
```typescript
// Send verification email
await authClient.sendVerificationEmail({
    email: "user@email.com",
    callbackURL: "/"
})

// Verify email with token
await authClient.verifyEmail({
    query: {
        token: "verification-token"
    }
})
```

**Server configuration:**
```typescript
export const auth = betterAuth({
    emailVerification: {
        sendVerificationEmail: async ({ user, url, token }, request) => {
            // Send verification email
        },
        sendOnSignUp: true, // Auto-send on signup
        autoSignInAfterVerification: true,
        afterEmailVerification: async (user, request) => {
            // Callback after successful verification
        }
    },
    emailAndPassword: {
        requireEmailVerification: true // Block login until verified
    }
})
```

---

### 4. Two-Factor Authentication (2FA)

**Client configuration:**
```typescript
import { twoFactorClient } from "better-auth/client/plugins"

const authClient = createAuthClient({
    plugins: [
        twoFactorClient({
            onTwoFactorRedirect() {
                window.location.href = "/2fa"
            }
        })
    ]
})
```

**Server configuration:**
```typescript
import { twoFactor } from "better-auth/plugins"

export const auth = betterAuth({
    appName: "My App", // Used as TOTP issuer
    plugins: [
        twoFactor({
            issuer: "my-app-name",
            otpOptions: {
                async sendOTP({ user, otp }, ctx) {
                    // Send OTP via email/SMS
                }
            }
        })
    ]
})
```

#### Enable/Disable 2FA
```typescript
// Enable 2FA - returns TOTP URI and backup codes
const { data } = await authClient.twoFactor.enable({
    password: "user-password"
})

// Disable 2FA
await authClient.twoFactor.disable({
    password: "user-password"
})
```

#### TOTP Verification
```typescript
// Get TOTP URI for QR code
await authClient.twoFactor.getTotpUri({ password })

// Verify TOTP code
await authClient.twoFactor.verifyTotp({
    code: "123456",
    trustDevice: true // Remember device for 30 days
})
```

#### OTP (Email/SMS) Verification
```typescript
// Send OTP
await authClient.twoFactor.sendOtp({
    trustDevice: true
})

// Verify OTP
await authClient.twoFactor.verifyOtp({
    code: "012345",
    trustDevice: true
})
```

#### Backup Codes
```typescript
// Generate new backup codes
await authClient.twoFactor.generateBackupCodes({
    password: "user-password"
})

// Verify with backup code
await authClient.twoFactor.verifyBackupCode({
    code: "123456",
    trustDevice: true
})
```

---

### 5. Session Management

#### Get Session
```typescript
// Client - hook (reactive)
const { data: session, isPending, error, refetch } = authClient.useSession()

// Client - one-time fetch
const { data: session } = await authClient.getSession()

// Server
const session = await auth.api.getSession({
    headers: await headers()
})
```

#### List Sessions
```typescript
const sessions = await authClient.listSessions()
```

#### Revoke Sessions
```typescript
// Revoke specific session
await authClient.revokeSession({
    token: "session-token"
})

// Revoke all other sessions (keep current)
await authClient.revokeOtherSessions()

// Revoke all sessions
await authClient.revokeSessions()
```

**Server configuration for session management:**
```typescript
export const auth = betterAuth({
    session: {
        expiresIn: 60 * 60 * 24 * 7, // 7 days
        updateAge: 60 * 60 * 24, // 1 day
        freshAge: 60 * 60 * 24, // 1 day - for "fresh session" checks
        disableSessionRefresh: false,
        cookieCache: {
            enabled: true,
            maxAge: 5 * 60, // 5 minutes
            strategy: "compact" // or "jwt" or "jwe"
        }
    }
})
```

---

### 6. Account Linking (OAuth Providers)

#### List Linked Accounts
```typescript
const accounts = await authClient.listAccounts()
```

#### Link Social Account
```typescript
// Standard OAuth flow
await authClient.linkSocial({
    provider: "google",
    callbackURL: "/callback"
})

// With custom scopes
await authClient.linkSocial({
    provider: "google",
    callbackURL: "/callback",
    scopes: ["https://www.googleapis.com/auth/drive.readonly"]
})

// With ID token (no redirect)
await authClient.linkSocial({
    provider: "google",
    idToken: {
        token: "id_token_from_provider",
        nonce: "nonce",
        accessToken: "access_token", // Optional
        refreshToken: "refresh_token" // Optional
    }
})
```

#### Unlink Account
```typescript
await authClient.unlinkAccount({
    providerId: "google"
})

// Unlink specific account (if multiple of same provider)
await authClient.unlinkAccount({
    providerId: "google",
    accountId: "123"
})
```

**Server configuration:**
```typescript
export const auth = betterAuth({
    account: {
        accountLinking: {
            enabled: true, // default
            trustedProviders: ["google", "github"], // Force-link trusted providers
            allowDifferentEmails: false,
            updateUserInfoOnLink: false,
            allowUnlinkingAll: false // Prevent account lockout
        }
    }
})
```

---

### 7. User Deletion

```typescript
await authClient.deleteUser({
    password: "password" // Required for credential users
})

// With callback URL
await authClient.deleteUser({
    callbackURL: "/goodbye"
})

// With verification token (for OAuth users)
await authClient.deleteUser({
    token: "verification-token"
})
```

**Server configuration:**
```typescript
export const auth = betterAuth({
    user: {
        deleteUser: {
            enabled: true,
            sendDeleteAccountVerification: async ({ user, url, token }, request) => {
                // Send deletion confirmation email
            },
            beforeDelete: async (user, request) => {
                // Pre-deletion cleanup
            },
            afterDelete: async (user, request) => {
                // Post-deletion cleanup
            }
        }
    }
})
```

---

### 8. Passkey Management

```typescript
// Add passkey
await authClient.passkey.addPasskey({
    name: "My Passkey"
})

// List passkeys
const { data } = authClient.useListPasskeys()

// Delete passkey
await authClient.passkey.deletePasskey({
    id: "passkey-id"
})
```

---

### 9. Polar Subscription Plugin

**Installation:**
```bash
pnpm add better-auth @polar-sh/better-auth @polar-sh/sdk
```

**Server configuration:**
```typescript
import { polar, checkout, portal, usage, webhooks } from "@polar-sh/better-auth"
import { Polar } from "@polar-sh/sdk"

const polarClient = new Polar({
    accessToken: process.env.POLAR_ACCESS_TOKEN,
    server: 'sandbox'
})

export const auth = betterAuth({
    plugins: [
        polar({
            client: polarClient,
            createCustomerOnSignUp: true,
            use: [
                checkout({
                    products: [{ productId: "123-456-789", slug: "pro" }],
                    successUrl: "/success?checkout_id={CHECKOUT_ID}",
                    authenticatedUsersOnly: true
                }),
                portal(),
                usage(),
                webhooks({
                    secret: process.env.POLAR_WEBHOOK_SECRET,
                    onCustomerStateChanged: (payload) => {},
                    onOrderPaid: (payload) => {},
                    onPayload: (payload) => {} // catch-all
                })
            ]
        })
    ]
